Dear Rob
Dear Louise,

many thanks for your helpful and fast answers! However a few specifications:

@Rob: There are current applications of using MRDS with dependent observers;  eg.
http://www.google.com/url?sa=t&rct=j&q=&esrc=s&source=web&cd=1&ved=0CCUQFjAA&url=http%3A%2F%2Firnr.tamu.edu%2Fmedia%2F294376%2Fpoint-based-mark-recapture-distance-sampling.pdf&ei=6hp2VJfxJM_voATpi4DYBw&usg=AFQjCNGJKrwFpiYXOTNOM2zzg_mq0Fb7RQ&sig2=YpbeFeok-vH2QcGNRqqEIQ&bvm=bv.80642063,d.cGU
Following that I would assume, that our approach would still be vaild for MRDS, hence it might be still difficult to generate a fully independent Observer 1 or accurate distance measurments by Observer 2.

@Louise: I have to clarify that we want to count animals and not scats (first because we have no defecation and decay rate estimates of the target species and second because the species can be seen realatively often in the field). Therefore the approach you described may not be valid for us, because the two observers would count different animals. Even if there are the same animals around, the distances would differ between the observers and it would be difficult do find similar groups.

So I guess that we have to stick on our dependent setting..

Thanks a lot for any further help!

Kindly,
Lukas

